            <div xml:id="d446">

                <pb facs="0567" n="555" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg555"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6353: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-31T20:00:00+02:00">October 31, 1940—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 31—6:02 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4549. Rumors that Germany will mediate between Greece and Italy are without
                    foundation according to the Greek Minister who believes that Greek-German
                    diplomatic relations will be broken shortly and that action to that end will
                    await the return of Ribbentrop whose arrival is expected today.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
